-- title:
--   Per-depth zero count at a supersingular node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke degeneracy maps, and a place specialisation $P$; let $R$ be a prolongation tuple for $P$, with $k$ perfect. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $w$ be a place of $k$-rational modular functions of level $N$, write $B := R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ for the ring of functions in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-modular functions of level $Nq$ that are integral for both prolongations $R_1, R_2$ and for every place above $w$ and whose Laurent expansion lies in the subfield generated over the constants of $K$ by $j$ and $j_{Nq}$, and let $\mathcal{O} := A \cap K$ with its constant embedding $\mathrm{nodeConst} : \mathcal{O} \to B$. Let $c$ be a system of node coordinates $x, y \in B$ (with the prescribed residues and orders $1$ at $w$ and at its Frobenius twist) and let $\varpi \in \mathcal{O}$ be nonzero. Assume: $B$ is local and Noetherian with maximal ideal $(\mathrm{nodeConst}\ \varpi, x, y)$; every $g \in B$ differs from some constant $\mathrm{nodeConst}\ o$ by a non-unit; $R$ satisfies the value-integrality law at $w$, namely that $V.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of any function integral at the node lies in $A$ for every place $V$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V = w$; $w$ is a supersingular place (rational, affine-geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set); $W$ is a complete discrete valuation domain with $\pi$ irreducible, $E \geq 1$, and $\iota$ is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $B$ onto the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^E)$ carrying $\mathrm{nodeConst}\ \varpi$ to the constant $\pi$ and $x$ to $U$ times a unit $\alpha_U$; every prime strictly below a non-maximal prime of $B$ is zero; every element of the said subfield is a ratio of elements of $B$; $\mathcal{O}$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$, and $\tau$ is an isomorphism of its adic completion with $W$ taking $\varpi$ to $\pi$ and compatible with $\iota$ on constants. Let $\mathfrak{q}$ be a prime of $B$ containing no nonzero constant $\mathrm{nodeConst}\ o$, let $f \in \mathfrak{q}$ be nonzero, let $r \geq 1$ and $p$ be natural numbers, and let $S$ be a finite set of places $V$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-modular functions of level $Nq$ such that each $V \in S$ reduces to $w$, has $\{g \in B : V.\mathrm{evalAt}\ g = 0\} = \mathfrak{q}$, and has $x$-depth satisfying $A.\mathrm{valuation}(V.\mathrm{evalAt}\ x)^r = A.\mathrm{valuation}(\varpi)^p$. Then, in $\mathbb{N}^\infty$, $\sum_{V \in S} (\mathrm{ord}_V f)^{+}$ is at most the length of $(B/fB)_{\mathfrak{q}}$ over $B_{\mathfrak{q}}$ times the sum of $\mathrm{finrank}_W$ of the quotients of the crossing model by those primes $Q$ which are minimal over the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{q}$ under $B \to \hat{B} \xrightarrow{\iota} W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$, do not contain the constant $\pi$, and satisfy $r \cdot \mathrm{length}_W(\text{model}/(Q + (U))) = p \cdot \mathrm{finrank}_W(\text{model}/Q)$.
--
--   This is the zero-counting inequality at a supersingular node refined by depth: the places above the node with a prescribed kernel of evaluation and prescribed rational depth $p/r$ are counted against the branches of the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ of the same depth, weighted by their $W$-ranks and by the local multiplicity of $f$ at $\mathfrak{q}$. It combines the per-kernel length identity for $\mathrm{ord}_V(f)$ with the cardinality bound for kernels of a given depth, and feeds the summation over depths in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.sum_ord_le_finsum_rank_mul_length_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.sum_ord_le_finsum_rank_mul_length_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel).
